# UI design standards

Apply these whenever adding or changing UI (components, pages, drawers, modals).

## Shape & borders

- **Nested radii:** inner `border-radius` = outer radius − padding (e.g. outer `16px`, padding `8px` → inner `8px`).
- **Borders:** prefer alpha blends, e.g. `border border-black/12` or `rgb(0 0 0 / 0.12)`, not heavy solid hex. In this repo, `border-border/50`–`/60` is the usual pattern on themed surfaces.

## Color & gradients

- **Palettes:** define new colors in **OKLCH** so equal L looks equal. Existing theme tokens in `globals.css` are HSL—when touching tokens or adding scales, prefer OKLCH.
- **Gradients:** use OKLCH interpolation: `linear-gradient(90deg in oklch, …)` (see `listingThumbColor.js` for inline gradient style).

## Typography & icons

- **Lucide icons:** match stroke to adjacent text—e.g. `strokeWidth={1.5}` near `text-sm font-medium`, slightly heavier for `font-semibold`/`text-base`.

## Scroll & carousels

- **Horizontal strips:** fade edges with  
  `mask-image: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, black 15%, black 85%, transparent)`  
  (and `-webkit-mask-image` when needed). Use for photo rails and snap carousels.

## Motion

- **Icon swaps:** blur outgoing icon while fading, e.g. `filter: blur(4px)` + opacity transition on the leaving element.

## Dark mode & layout

- **Depth in dark UI:** lift hierarchy with **lighter surface steps** (`bg-card`, `bg-muted/…`); don’t rely on shadows alone.
- **Full viewport height:** use `min-h-[100dvh]` / `h-[100dvh]`, not `100vh` (Safari).

## Product imagery

- **White-background shots:** `mix-blend-mode: multiply` on the image so white merges with the surface.

## Tailwind shortcuts

```tsx
// Nested radius (Tailwind arbitrary)
className="rounded-2xl p-2 [&>*]:rounded-xl" // 16px − 8px = 8px on child

// Carousel fade
style={{
  WebkitMaskImage:
    "linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, black 15%, black 85%, transparent)",
  maskImage:
    "linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, black 15%, black 85%, transparent)",
}}
```